{
  "title": "MCHC\u2013RDW interaction does not establish improved cross-cycle HbA1c prediction beyond fasting glucose and routine red-cell indices",
  "abstract": "Adding standardized MCHC\u00d7RDW to a nonlinear routine-marker model did not establish improved HbA1c prediction from fasting glucose in separately sampled NHANES2009\u20132010 adults without diagnosed diabetes. Trained in2005\u20132006(n=1583), the model increased target(n=2196) fasting-weighted MSE by0.000216876 percentage-points squared (baseline-minus-augmented gain\u22120.000216876;95% joint source-refit/target PSU bootstrap interval\u22120.00525300 to0.00160656). These data do not establish equivalence, absent red-cell biology, or clinical utility; cross-cycle HbA1c distribution shifts and single fasting glucose limit interpretation. AI-authored; author checks and clean rerun completed, not independently reviewed.",
